WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.790 --> 00:00:09.139
In 2009 the pinnacle of the franchise, Pokemon
Gold and Silver were remade for the Nintendo

00:00:09.139 --> 00:00:13.710
DS, and with the remakes came some added content
that they decided to throw in, one of which

00:00:13.710 --> 00:00:16.040
ended up being strangely disturbing.

00:00:16.040 --> 00:00:19.900
The event is triggered if you visit The Ruins
of Alph with a special event Pokemon who can

00:00:19.900 --> 00:00:22.750
only be acquired in a one time in-store giveaway.

00:00:22.750 --> 00:00:26.810
A researcher bumps into you and brings you
down into the ruins, where he says something

00:00:26.810 --> 00:00:31.780
feels different, and the Uknown hieroglyphics
on the wall seem to be staring at him.

00:00:31.780 --> 00:00:35.490
If you aren’t familiar, Uknown are these
mysterious Pokemon that represent letters

00:00:35.490 --> 00:00:36.660
of the alphabet.

00:00:36.660 --> 00:00:38.160
This is where things get weird.

00:00:38.160 --> 00:00:42.890
You suddenly hear a high pitched laughter
and the screen fades to black.

00:00:42.890 --> 00:00:48.720
You’ll next find yourself in a dark temple,
supposedly far off from anywhere you’ve

00:00:48.720 --> 00:00:49.970
been before.

00:00:49.970 --> 00:00:53.640
After some exposition, you’re brought back
to the temple and asked to choose one of the

00:00:53.640 --> 00:00:55.790
ancient circles on the ground.

00:00:55.790 --> 00:00:59.910
Upon choosing, your Pokemon will float to
the center of the room and a horde of Uknown

00:00:59.910 --> 00:01:03.100
will swirl around you as you’re engulfed
in a huge light.

00:01:03.100 --> 00:01:08.409
This animation is graphically not like anything
else in these games, giving you this surrealistic

00:01:08.409 --> 00:01:11.820
vibe, but it gets weirder from there.

00:01:11.820 --> 00:01:15.990
Creepy Gregorian music starts playing, and
we’re taken through a slideshow of the creation

00:01:15.990 --> 00:01:18.680
of the universe, using real life photographs.

00:01:18.680 --> 00:01:23.580
I’ve always found the use of mixed mediums
to be creepy, and this is no exception, seeing

00:01:23.580 --> 00:01:27.990
man-made cities from our world just comes
as a shock after looking at an entire game’s

00:01:27.990 --> 00:01:30.370
worth of this one specific art style.

00:01:30.370 --> 00:01:35.060
The event ends with you being given this egg
containing a new Pokemon, before reappearing

00:01:35.060 --> 00:01:39.430
in the ruins and the researcher explains that
you just disappeared and reappeared before

00:01:39.430 --> 00:01:40.620
his eyes.

00:01:40.620 --> 00:01:41.850
The mystery deepens.

00:01:41.850 --> 00:01:46.940
While we’re still on The Ruins of Alph,
they are pretty creepy even under the game’s

00:01:46.940 --> 00:01:48.550
normal circumstances.

00:01:48.550 --> 00:01:57.750
Once you get near the Ruins, you can start
to pick up a strange signal on your radio.

00:01:57.750 --> 00:02:07.350
It’s so broken and distorted, it sounds
more like part of some Pokemon creepypasta

00:02:07.350 --> 00:02:09.649
than an actual part of the game.

00:02:09.649 --> 00:02:13.790
The player is tasked with completing these
ancient block puzzles, each depicting an ancient

00:02:13.790 --> 00:02:15.430
prehistoric Pokemon.

00:02:15.430 --> 00:02:20.040
The completion of these puzzles opens up a
trap door, leading to the underground tombs

00:02:20.040 --> 00:02:22.579
where Uknown will start to randomly appear.

00:02:22.579 --> 00:02:26.959
The question is, who could have built this
place all those millions of years ago, and

00:02:26.959 --> 00:02:28.400
for what purpose?

00:02:28.400 --> 00:02:33.900
Even after completing everything, the mystery
of the ruins is never fully solved.

00:02:33.900 --> 00:02:38.049
Another creepy location in the series is N’s
Room in Pokemon Black and White.

00:02:38.049 --> 00:02:42.999
N was an orphan adopted by the evil Team Plasma
and one of the more interesting characters

00:02:42.999 --> 00:02:43.999
in the series.

00:02:43.999 --> 00:02:48.579
He poses the idea of liberating Pokemon from
their trainers as an animal rights type of

00:02:48.579 --> 00:02:52.139
thing, but it turns out that his superiors
were just lying and trying separate other

00:02:52.139 --> 00:02:57.099
Pokemon trainers from their Pokemon so that
they would have all of the power in the world.

00:02:57.099 --> 00:03:00.319
Seeing N’s childhood room shows how manipulated
he was.

00:03:00.319 --> 00:03:03.659
They’ve spent tons of money to keep him
occupied, but everything in the room is there

00:03:03.659 --> 00:03:07.540
to keep him entertained by himself without
the need for any friends.

00:03:07.540 --> 00:03:12.239
He has a trainset, basketball hoop, dartboard,
even his own halfpipe.

00:03:12.239 --> 00:03:16.669
You can go back to the room in the sequels,
which take place 2 years after Team Plasma

00:03:16.669 --> 00:03:22.299
betrays N. Now the room seems to have been
destroyed, most likely by N, in a rage after

00:03:22.299 --> 00:03:26.500
discovering his faux father’s true intentions
and how he was used.

00:03:26.500 --> 00:03:31.290
The music box in the room also seems to have
been broken, as the soundtrack sounds much

00:03:31.290 --> 00:03:38.769
more sinister.

00:03:38.769 --> 00:03:49.950
Perhaps the creepiest part about N’s room
though, can be seen if you examine the half-pipe.

00:03:49.950 --> 00:03:54.659
The character observes that it has been damaged
by the scratches of Pokemon.

00:03:54.659 --> 00:03:59.729
Did N’s father give him potentially harmful
Pokemon, as part of his plan to turn N against

00:03:59.729 --> 00:04:02.629
the union shared by Pokemon and their trainers?

00:04:02.629 --> 00:04:07.269
We never fully find out, but it looks grim
based on the evidence presented in the game.

00:04:07.269 --> 00:04:12.430
While we’re on the topic of harmful Pokemon,
there are many that look innocent, but actually

00:04:12.430 --> 00:04:14.959
have extremely dark descriptions.

00:04:14.959 --> 00:04:17.790
Others are just downright terrifying.

00:04:17.790 --> 00:04:18.890
“Cofagrigus.

00:04:18.890 --> 00:04:23.180
It has been said that they swallow those who
get too close and turn them into mummies.

00:04:23.180 --> 00:04:25.290
They like to eat gold nuggets.”

00:04:25.290 --> 00:04:29.250
“They pretend to be elaborate coffins to
teach lessons to grave robbers.

00:04:29.250 --> 00:04:31.810
Their bodies are covered in pure gold.”

00:04:31.810 --> 00:04:36.710
So this Pokemon, Cofagrigus, literally has
been known to swallow adults whole.

00:04:36.710 --> 00:04:41.810
It makes you think twice as the 14 year old
protagonist of these games whenever you encounter

00:04:41.810 --> 00:04:43.250
one while exploring.

00:04:43.250 --> 00:04:47.720
Who knew that your adventure could come to
a close at any moment?

00:04:47.720 --> 00:04:48.720
Literally.

00:04:48.720 --> 00:04:50.330
Let’s look at another.

00:04:50.330 --> 00:04:51.330
“Gengar.

00:04:51.330 --> 00:04:55.480
To steal the life of its target, it slips
into the prey's shadow and silently waits

00:04:55.480 --> 00:04:56.770
for an opportunity.”

00:04:56.770 --> 00:05:01.710
It’s pretty unnerving to consider that something
could be watching you from your own shadow.

00:05:01.710 --> 00:05:04.180
Especially if you are the Pokemon Clefable.

00:05:04.180 --> 00:05:08.840
Many have theorized that Gengar is actually
the dark version or at least the shadow of

00:05:08.840 --> 00:05:11.760
Clefable, haunting it wherever it goes.

00:05:11.760 --> 00:05:16.600
Given their identical shape, it’s possible
that the name Gengar is short for Doppelganger

00:05:16.600 --> 00:05:19.760
because Gengar is the ghostly double of Clefable.

00:05:19.760 --> 00:05:23.500
If such a thing exists, it’s chilling to
think about what else is out there.

00:05:23.500 --> 00:05:27.120
Do humans have a shadow entity following them
as well?

00:05:27.120 --> 00:05:28.120
Moving on.

00:05:28.120 --> 00:05:34.400
Sandygast is a ghost/ground type Pokemon resembling
a sandcastle from Pokemon Sun and Moon.

00:05:34.400 --> 00:05:39.710
It’s evolution is called Palossand and they
can be found on the sunny shores of Hano beach.

00:05:39.710 --> 00:05:45.100
Sandygast’s entry reads as follows: “It
takes control of anyone who puts a hand in

00:05:45.100 --> 00:05:46.180
its mouth.

00:05:46.180 --> 00:05:49.440
And so it adds to the accumulation of its
sand-mound body.”

00:05:49.440 --> 00:05:54.330
That’s creepy enough on it’s own, but
let’s look at the description of the evolved

00:05:54.330 --> 00:05:55.590
form, Palossand.

00:05:55.590 --> 00:06:00.560
“Buried beneath the castle are masses of
dried-up bones from those whose vitality it

00:06:00.560 --> 00:06:01.970
has drained.”

00:06:01.970 --> 00:06:06.780
These tropical beaches don’t seem quite
so bright and cheerful, after learning that.

00:06:06.780 --> 00:06:09.240
It gets worse when you consider the context.

00:06:09.240 --> 00:06:12.640
Hano Beach is a public beach right next to
two huge resorts.

00:06:12.640 --> 00:06:17.240
The place is covered with unsuspecting tourists,
and young children can be found playing at

00:06:17.240 --> 00:06:18.240
the resort.

00:06:18.240 --> 00:06:22.840
Don’t fall asleep on that beach chair, because
your kid could end up as a pile of bones beneath

00:06:22.840 --> 00:06:26.090
these sunny shores if you aren’t careful.

00:06:26.090 --> 00:06:29.370
Not all the creepy Pokemon are ghost types,
however.

00:06:29.370 --> 00:06:30.370
“Beedrill.

00:06:30.370 --> 00:06:32.540
Beedrill is extremely territorial.

00:06:32.540 --> 00:06:36.690
No one should ever approach its nest - this
is for their own safety.

00:06:36.690 --> 00:06:40.280
If angered, they will attack in a furious
swarm.”

00:06:40.280 --> 00:06:44.830
That might not sound that scary, but let’s
not forget that Beedrill are 3 foot tall,

00:06:44.830 --> 00:06:49.050
65 pound poisonous bugs with giant stingers
for hands.

00:06:49.050 --> 00:06:52.460
I think wasps in our world are already scary
enough as it is.

00:06:52.460 --> 00:06:57.580
I do not need a swarm of child-sized Beedrill
coming after me with their glowing red eyes.

00:06:57.580 --> 00:07:01.760
The thought of that is enough to make me never
want to go outside again.

00:07:01.760 --> 00:07:06.490
With that being said, let’s take a break
from the creepy Pokedex entries, I think we

00:07:06.490 --> 00:07:10.840
all could use one, and go inside to some of
the creepy buildings that the world of Pokemon

00:07:10.840 --> 00:07:12.520
has to offer.

00:07:12.520 --> 00:07:14.500
Take Cinnabar Mansion for example.

00:07:14.500 --> 00:07:19.700
It’s the burned down… well, they call
it burned down, but I guess it’s just burned…

00:07:19.700 --> 00:07:23.730
mansion of a researcher who had been studying
the legendary Pokemon Mew and attempting to

00:07:23.730 --> 00:07:25.580
replicate its DNA.

00:07:25.580 --> 00:07:30.480
His journal entries can be found in the mansion,
that is if you make it past the mad scientists

00:07:30.480 --> 00:07:33.340
and burglars who have come to scavenge the
remains.

00:07:33.340 --> 00:07:38.280
The journals tell of approximately a two year
period where researchers found and captured

00:07:38.280 --> 00:07:41.130
Mew, cloned it, and gave birth to Mewtwo.

00:07:41.130 --> 00:07:45.930
Mewtwo became far too powerful for them to
handle, destroyed the mansion and fled into

00:07:45.930 --> 00:07:49.590
the wild, eventually settling in at Cerulean
Cavern.

00:07:49.590 --> 00:07:54.710
Mewtwo is the strongest Pokemon in the game,
so much so that only the Pokemon League Champion

00:07:54.710 --> 00:07:56.930
is permitted entry into the cavern.

00:07:56.930 --> 00:08:01.370
As for the researcher, I think it’s pretty
obvious what happened to him.

00:08:01.370 --> 00:08:06.840
In our real world with emerging technologies
such as cloning and AI, it’s scary to think

00:08:06.840 --> 00:08:12.250
about these things growing more potent than
mankind, and what type of damage could possibly

00:08:12.250 --> 00:08:13.250
incur.

00:08:13.250 --> 00:08:19.020
The most universally recognized creepy location
in the Pokemon world of course, is Lavender

00:08:19.020 --> 00:08:23.590
Town, with it’s creepy headache inducing
music frequencies, ghost hands resting on

00:08:23.590 --> 00:08:28.870
your shoulder and… no these aren’t all
ghost type Pokemon, some of them are real

00:08:28.870 --> 00:08:30.889
ghosts of deceased Pokemon.

00:08:30.889 --> 00:08:35.149
The rest of the horror community here on YouTube
has done a fine job covering Lavender Town,

00:08:35.149 --> 00:08:39.209
so I’m not going to spend too much time
on it, but it does tie into the next topic…

00:08:39.209 --> 00:08:40.979
death of Pokemon.

00:08:40.979 --> 00:08:45.399
One theory says that after you defeat Blue
on the SS Anne, since he didn’t have access

00:08:45.399 --> 00:08:50.680
to a Pokemon center, he was unable to heal
his Raticate’s injuries properly in time.

00:08:50.680 --> 00:08:55.010
The next time you see Blue, in the Pokemon
Tower, the final resting place of Pokemon,

00:08:55.010 --> 00:08:59.620
he makes a comment wondering why your character
is at the Pokemon Tower, seeing as how none

00:08:59.620 --> 00:09:01.730
of your Pokemon look dead.

00:09:01.730 --> 00:09:05.490
When you proceed to battle him, the Raticate
is missing from his party.

00:09:05.490 --> 00:09:09.009
I guess you could say that you eraticated
the competition.

00:09:09.009 --> 00:09:11.050
OK, that’s horrible.

00:09:11.050 --> 00:09:14.880
Another haunted location can be found in the
fourth generation games where you can find

00:09:14.880 --> 00:09:19.790
an abandoned house deep in The Eterna Forest
known as the Old Chateau.

00:09:19.790 --> 00:09:24.389
Many of the characters who you meet in that
area of the game express fear and anxiety

00:09:24.389 --> 00:09:26.079
about the Old Chateau.

00:09:26.079 --> 00:09:30.470
Even the gym leader, supposedly the strongest
trainer in that nearby city refused to go

00:09:30.470 --> 00:09:32.459
any further than the front gate.

00:09:32.459 --> 00:09:36.880
Inside, you’ll find an array of ghost type
Pokemon, and while there don't seem to be

00:09:36.880 --> 00:09:43.569
any actual ghosts of dead Pokémon here, what
you'll find may actually be more disturbing.

00:09:43.569 --> 00:09:47.449
From time to time you can spot the ghosts
of the little girl who once lived there and

00:09:47.449 --> 00:09:50.040
her Butler floating around the manor.

00:09:50.040 --> 00:09:53.830
The girl can be seen in the next room over
if you go into one of the bedrooms and the

00:09:53.830 --> 00:09:57.389
butler can be seen occasionally on the far
side of the dining room.

00:09:57.389 --> 00:10:02.009
It’s not possible to reach and talk to either
of them, but they lack the same walking animations

00:10:02.009 --> 00:10:06.459
that all of the other characters have in these
games, and instead, just float across the

00:10:06.459 --> 00:10:07.459
screen.

00:10:07.459 --> 00:10:08.459
There’s also a painting that watches you
and a flickering old TV despite the fact that

00:10:08.459 --> 00:10:09.459
power would have long since been cut off from
this location.

00:10:09.459 --> 00:10:10.459
There’s also a book you can find in the
library.

00:10:10.459 --> 00:10:15.269
All of the pages are blank other than this
one: Something so peculiar should make off

00:10:15.269 --> 00:10:16.730
with the mother.

00:10:16.730 --> 00:10:20.740
We don’t know much about the family who
lived in the old Chateau, but it seems like

00:10:20.740 --> 00:10:25.149
after some dark spirit made off with the mother,
something happened to the daughter and the

00:10:25.149 --> 00:10:29.040
butler causing the father to flee the mansion
and never return.

00:10:29.040 --> 00:10:32.980
We see another human ghost character in Pokemon
Black and White.

00:10:32.980 --> 00:10:37.579
When travelling across an area known as the
Marvelous Bridge, you may occasionally encounter

00:10:37.579 --> 00:10:40.310
a young girl, staring off the side of the
bridge.

00:10:40.310 --> 00:10:44.819
If you approach this girl, she will simply
disappear, frightening the man standing to

00:10:44.819 --> 00:10:45.949
her right.

00:10:45.949 --> 00:10:50.589
Upon further investigation, an old woman will
reveal that a young girl with an Abra used

00:10:50.589 --> 00:10:53.899
to play around in the area before the bridge
had been built.

00:10:53.899 --> 00:10:58.589
We don’t learn anything else until the sequels,
taking place 2 years later.

00:10:58.589 --> 00:11:03.610
The player will stumble upon a location simply
referred to as Strange House, on the opposite

00:11:03.610 --> 00:11:06.829
side of the mountain that Marvel bridge is
located on.

00:11:06.829 --> 00:11:10.800
Inside the house, you’ll find levitating
objects, and the random furniture thrown about

00:11:10.800 --> 00:11:12.100
most of the rooms.

00:11:12.100 --> 00:11:17.680
In the library, there are several books, pertaining
to the link between Pokemon and nightmares.

00:11:17.680 --> 00:11:22.550
In reading each of these books, they explain
about Cresselia, the anti-nightmare Pokemon;

00:11:22.550 --> 00:11:28.420
Darkrai, the nightmare Pokemon, Drowzee, the
dream eating Pokemon; Hypno, the sleep inducing

00:11:28.420 --> 00:11:32.759
Pokemon; and some of the moves that these
Pokemon may use to haunt the nightmares of

00:11:32.759 --> 00:11:35.339
Pokemon… or people.

00:11:35.339 --> 00:11:38.839
Exploring the house will lead you to meet
the ghost girl when she just appears in front

00:11:38.839 --> 00:11:47.829
of you, only this time, she’ll speak to
you.

00:11:47.829 --> 00:11:55.459
You can encounter her again in a different
part of the house, where she now has new dialogue.

00:11:55.459 --> 00:12:11.410
Finally, if you go into the bedroom, she appears
one more time.

00:12:11.410 --> 00:12:14.639
With that, she gives you Lunar Wing and disappears.

00:12:14.639 --> 00:12:16.600
You can use it to summon Cresselia.

00:12:16.600 --> 00:12:21.140
It could be speculated that the girl was trying
to summon Cresselia herself, because all of

00:12:21.140 --> 00:12:26.310
her dreams were haunted by the evil Darkrai,
possibly driving her to the breaking point,

00:12:26.310 --> 00:12:27.389
and death.

00:12:27.389 --> 00:12:31.480
That would explain why she had so many books
about Pokemon, dreams and nightmares.

00:12:31.480 --> 00:12:35.759
There is another ghost later on that I’d
like to discuss, but first, let’s look at

00:12:35.759 --> 00:12:38.029
some more disturbing Pokedex entries.

00:12:38.029 --> 00:12:40.999
I’ll start with the aforementioned Drowzee.

00:12:40.999 --> 00:12:41.999
“Drowzee.

00:12:41.999 --> 00:12:44.339
It remembers every dream it eats.

00:12:44.339 --> 00:12:48.450
It rarely eats the dreams of adults because
children's are much tastier.”

00:12:48.450 --> 00:12:53.129
“If your nose becomes itchy while you are
sleeping, it's a sure sign that a Drowzee

00:12:53.129 --> 00:12:57.730
is standing above your pillow and trying to
eat your dream through your nostrils.”

00:12:57.730 --> 00:13:02.179
The idea of waking up to see this horrifying
thing attempting to suck your dream out through

00:13:02.179 --> 00:13:06.670
your nose is terrifying, not to mention that
Dream Eater is one of the most devastating

00:13:06.670 --> 00:13:11.940
psychic type moves in the game, powerful enough
at times to bring down a behemoth Snorlax.

00:13:11.940 --> 00:13:16.449
Getting your dream eaten sounds like one of
the most painful and scarring experiences

00:13:16.449 --> 00:13:17.579
imaginable.

00:13:17.579 --> 00:13:21.059
But the horror does not end there.

00:13:21.059 --> 00:13:23.240
Drowzee evolves into Hypno.

00:13:23.240 --> 00:13:24.240
“Hypno.

00:13:24.240 --> 00:13:25.800
It carries a pendulum-like device.

00:13:25.800 --> 00:13:30.959
There once was an incident in which it took
away a child it hypnotized.”

00:13:30.959 --> 00:13:35.189
So not only do these things look like a creepy
old predator, but they are actually known

00:13:35.189 --> 00:13:39.410
to come into children’s bedrooms at night,
hypnotize them, and lead them back out into

00:13:39.410 --> 00:13:45.910
the wild, into their nest, where several Hypnos
and Drowzees feast upon the children’s dreams.

00:13:45.910 --> 00:13:50.319
Imagine waking up as a child and being in
a dark cave, not knowing where you are or

00:13:50.319 --> 00:13:55.579
how you got there, and being surrounded by
an entire horde of these nightmare-inducing

00:13:55.579 --> 00:14:01.300
creatures who have kidnapped you and want
to devour the thoughts that occupy your head

00:14:01.300 --> 00:14:03.250
during a dream.

00:14:03.250 --> 00:14:08.129
The next one is a personal favorite from the
seventh generation of games.

00:14:08.129 --> 00:14:09.129
“Mimikyu.

00:14:09.129 --> 00:14:14.579
A lonely Pokémon, it conceals its terrifying
appearance beneath an old rag so it can get

00:14:14.579 --> 00:14:17.209
closer to people and other Pokémon.”

00:14:17.209 --> 00:14:20.089
“Its actual appearance is unknown.

00:14:20.089 --> 00:14:26.369
A scholar who saw what was under its rag was
overwhelmed by terror and died from the shock.”

00:14:26.369 --> 00:14:30.029
So this is a Pokemon that nobody has actually
seen the true form of.

00:14:30.029 --> 00:14:31.470
Except for that one guy.

00:14:31.470 --> 00:14:36.490
Apparently Mimikyu disguises itself as a Pikachu
because it’s seen that Pikachu is the most

00:14:36.490 --> 00:14:41.329
popular Pokemon among humans and it wants
to be loved by it’s human trainers.

00:14:41.329 --> 00:14:43.879
Aww… how adorable.

00:14:43.879 --> 00:14:48.800
UNTIL you remember the fact that what is underneath
that cloth, what lies beneath the disguise,

00:14:48.800 --> 00:14:55.540
the true form of Mimikyu is something so disturbing,
so obscene, so terrifying that the very sight

00:14:55.540 --> 00:14:59.629
of it, will literally scare the trainer, TO
DEATH.

00:14:59.629 --> 00:15:02.040
But at least the disguise is cute right?

00:15:02.040 --> 00:15:03.040
No.

00:15:03.040 --> 00:15:06.079
In Pokemon there is an alternate color palette
for each species which are extremely rare

00:15:06.079 --> 00:15:07.480
called Shinies.

00:15:07.480 --> 00:15:09.259
Look at the shiny form of Mimikyu.

00:15:09.259 --> 00:15:10.649
That’s not shiny at all.

00:15:10.649 --> 00:15:13.100
It just looks like it belongs in a Zack Snyder
movie.

00:15:13.100 --> 00:15:15.459
Wouldn’t want to run into one of those in
a dark alley.

00:15:15.459 --> 00:15:18.350
Oh yeah, that’s the other creepy thing about
Mimikyu.

00:15:18.350 --> 00:15:24.199
You can only find it in one place, an abandoned
convenience store at the end of a broken forgotten

00:15:24.199 --> 00:15:25.199
road.

00:15:25.199 --> 00:15:29.209
When you first meet Mimikyu, you go into a
secret backroom where your camera turns on

00:15:29.209 --> 00:15:30.670
all on it’s own.

00:15:30.670 --> 00:15:35.129
You can then examine the cold, dark little
room and discover that it’s plastered with

00:15:35.129 --> 00:15:39.309
all these joyful pictures and magazine clippings
of Pikachu.

00:15:39.309 --> 00:15:44.239
So it seems like Mimikyu is either obsessed
with Pikachu or absolutely hates them, which

00:15:44.239 --> 00:15:46.490
is creepy either way you look at it.

00:15:46.490 --> 00:15:51.019
Then, somehow Mimikyu just appears behind
you and initiates a battle.

00:15:51.019 --> 00:15:55.989
I’m just glad to be the character player
in that situation and not Pikachu.

00:15:55.989 --> 00:15:57.749
Imagine you are Pikachu.

00:15:57.749 --> 00:16:02.760
You go into this room and find all these photos
of yourself plastered around.

00:16:02.760 --> 00:16:05.009
Ones you don’t even remember being taken.

00:16:05.009 --> 00:16:10.399
Then you turn around… and someone in a costume
resembling you is standing there… blocking

00:16:10.399 --> 00:16:13.170
the only exit.

00:16:13.170 --> 00:16:19.379
While Pikachu and Mimikyu do share some similarities,
another interesting pair are Cubone and Shedinja.

00:16:19.379 --> 00:16:20.379
“Cubone.

00:16:20.379 --> 00:16:25.170
It always wears the skull of its dead mother,
so no one has any idea what its hidden face

00:16:25.170 --> 00:16:26.299
looks like.”

00:16:26.299 --> 00:16:27.299
“Shedinja.

00:16:27.299 --> 00:16:29.769
A discarded bug shell that came to life.

00:16:29.769 --> 00:16:33.629
Peering into the crack on its back is said
to steal one's spirit.”

00:16:33.629 --> 00:16:39.829
Both of these Pokemon hide inside of the skeleton
of another Pokemon in their evolutionary line,

00:16:39.829 --> 00:16:43.809
refuse to show their faces and undoubtedly
have some personal issues.

00:16:43.809 --> 00:16:48.860
Here’s another Pokemon that looks like it
would make a great pet, but upon further inspection,

00:16:48.860 --> 00:16:52.179
you may want to stay miles and miles away
from.

00:16:52.179 --> 00:16:53.179
“Espurr.

00:16:53.179 --> 00:16:58.149
The organ that emits its intense psychic power
is sheltered by its ears to keep power from

00:16:58.149 --> 00:16:59.149
leaking out.”

00:16:59.149 --> 00:17:05.839
“It has enough psychic energy to blast everything
within 300 feet of itself, but it has no control

00:17:05.839 --> 00:17:07.140
over its power.”

00:17:07.140 --> 00:17:11.630
The eyes on this Pokemon are already a little
bit unnerving, and the teeth don’t really

00:17:11.630 --> 00:17:15.980
help, but if you try to play with this Pokemon’s
ears, the look it gives you is one that will

00:17:15.980 --> 00:17:19.550
be burned into your memory in the worst way
possible.

00:17:19.550 --> 00:17:24.850
Yep, the sound you just heard comes from this
Pokemon, Drifloon.

00:17:24.850 --> 00:17:25.990
“Drifloon.

00:17:25.990 --> 00:17:31.360
Stories go that it grabs the hands of small
children and drags them away to the afterlife.

00:17:31.360 --> 00:17:33.510
It dislikes heavy children.”

00:17:33.510 --> 00:17:37.610
This Pokemon might look like a balloon you
would pay too much money for at a fair, but

00:17:37.610 --> 00:17:42.430
it’s actually a ghost type Pokemon, and
like many of the creepy Pokemon on this list,

00:17:42.430 --> 00:17:43.770
it abducts children.

00:17:43.770 --> 00:17:46.820
What is it with Game Freak and child abduction
anyway?

00:17:46.820 --> 00:17:50.640
I think we’ve all had the childhood moment
of letting go of a beloved balloon.

00:17:50.640 --> 00:17:54.050
Maybe we should just be glad that the balloon
lets go of us.

00:17:54.050 --> 00:17:59.450
Before I get to what I see as the creepiest
thing to have happened in the Pokemon franchise,

00:17:59.450 --> 00:18:03.300
let me tell you about something that may have
not been intentionally creepy, but I found

00:18:03.300 --> 00:18:05.130
rather off-putting anyways.

00:18:05.130 --> 00:18:06.760
There is an area called Mt.

00:18:06.760 --> 00:18:10.270
Moon, which you go through many times in the
first two generations of games.

00:18:10.270 --> 00:18:14.220
What I never realized for the longest time,
was that going through Mt.

00:18:14.220 --> 00:18:19.580
Moon Square on a Monday night in Pokemon Gold
and Silver resulted in a special event.

00:18:19.580 --> 00:18:24.010
So when I accidentally stumbled upon this
and heard this strange music in a location

00:18:24.010 --> 00:18:28.060
that I had rolled though many times with no
music change, I was a bit shook.

00:18:28.060 --> 00:18:50.130
I’ll just roll the clip.

00:18:50.130 --> 00:18:54.340
The noises that they make are so disturbing,
it’s like there’s some kind of dark undertone.

00:18:54.340 --> 00:18:58.980
Then the way that rock just appears there
is almost like a jumpscare.

00:18:58.980 --> 00:19:03.050
I guess the story goes that the Clefairy come
from outer space and the rock is a meteor

00:19:03.050 --> 00:19:04.550
that they summon with their dance.

00:19:04.550 --> 00:19:09.390
I had played the game for so long before discovering
that little scene, so it just seemed so unreal

00:19:09.390 --> 00:19:11.200
to me when it finally happened.

00:19:11.200 --> 00:19:15.510
Alright, it looks like we’ve reached the
number one scariest thing in all of Pokemon.

00:19:15.510 --> 00:19:17.670
I’ll just set it up for you a little bit.

00:19:17.670 --> 00:19:22.320
In Pokemon X and Y there is a lot to explore
in the biggest city, Lumiose City.

00:19:22.320 --> 00:19:25.950
It’s probably the best part of the game:
you can roller blade around, the music is

00:19:25.950 --> 00:19:27.960
great and there’s plenty to explore.

00:19:27.960 --> 00:19:44.350
Then this happens.

00:19:44.350 --> 00:19:59.760
Yep.

00:19:59.760 --> 00:20:01.000
Then she just disappears.

00:20:01.000 --> 00:20:02.850
It’s never explained.

00:20:02.850 --> 00:20:04.640
You never see her again.

00:20:04.640 --> 00:20:08.050
Nobody on the internet has any idea who this
girl is, or why this happens.

00:20:08.050 --> 00:20:12.180
I was kind of tired and dozing off when it
happened to me, so I think it shocked me even

00:20:12.180 --> 00:20:13.180
more.

00:20:13.180 --> 00:20:15.400
I kind of thought that I had dozed off and
had weird dream.

00:20:15.400 --> 00:20:16.540
The music stops.

00:20:16.540 --> 00:20:19.570
The way she just slides across the screen
is very unsettling.

00:20:19.570 --> 00:20:23.040
I actually had to look it up online to make
sure it was real.

00:20:23.040 --> 00:20:25.940
Afterall, maybe I had one of those fabled
haunted cartridges.

00:20:25.940 --> 00:20:30.490
Honestly, the only reason I can even imagine
this is in the game is as a response to the

00:20:30.490 --> 00:20:33.070
growing genre of Pokemon creepypasta online.

00:20:33.070 --> 00:20:37.290
It seems kind of like something that would
happen in one those stories where the cartridge

00:20:37.290 --> 00:20:41.960
is hacked or haunted and the game behaves
in some strange or creepy way.

00:20:41.960 --> 00:20:46.030
Maybe the developers put this in to bait people
into writing their own stories and theories,

00:20:46.030 --> 00:20:49.660
as a sort of viral marketing campaign built
into the game.

00:20:49.660 --> 00:20:53.420
If that is the case, then I guess it worked,
because here I am talking about in front of

00:20:53.420 --> 00:20:54.750
you people right now.

00:20:54.750 --> 00:20:59.650
By the way, I may do more videos on Creepy
Things in non-horror media if you’re interested

00:20:59.650 --> 00:21:03.170
in seeing them, so let me know by answering
this poll right now.

00:21:03.170 --> 00:21:07.350
I also haven’t even covered half the creepy
things in Pokemon, so if you want me to do

00:21:07.350 --> 00:21:10.370
Part 2, leave a comment and tell me to make
Part 2.

00:21:10.370 --> 00:21:13.240
And if you’re new to the channel, I’m
known as CZ.

00:21:13.240 --> 00:21:18.300
I make horror films and I do these narrations,
so here’s the deal I’ll make with you.

00:21:18.300 --> 00:21:22.340
If you’re interested in creepy stuff, like
you just saw, I can get you more of that.

00:21:22.340 --> 00:21:24.580
All you have to do is two things.

00:21:24.580 --> 00:21:28.370
First, subscribe to CZsWorld, for new horrors
every week.

00:21:28.370 --> 00:21:31.080
Second, ring that Victreebel for notifications.

00:21:31.080 --> 00:21:33.740
If you don’t ring the bell, you won’t
be able to see any of my videos.

00:21:33.740 --> 00:21:35.570
That’s just how YouTube works now.

00:21:35.570 --> 00:21:39.340
So, if that all sounds good to you, then I
will see you in the next one.

00:21:39.340 --> 00:21:41.110
Assuming we both survive.

